  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. RNA is clearly dominant (0.48–0.65) while image alone is weak (0.21 with resnet50). scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the strongest RNA setup, and transformer ≈ avgpool (0.653 vs 0.650). Key uncertainty: whether adding image features to this strong RNA baseline provides complementary signal that improves accuracy, or whether the weak image (0.21) dilutes the RNA signal. This experiment (config_032) directly extends the best RNA-only result by adding resnet50 image features via concat fusion in the multiprofile+transformer setting, isolating the effect of multimodal fusion. It is the most logical single-step exploitation of our strongest evidence. With 3 experiments remaining after this, a positive result would justify further multimodal exploration; a null/negative result would confirm RNA-only multiprofile as the ceiling and allow the remaining budget to focus on RNA-side refinements."
}

